  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_006: rna_only, pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool → 59.1% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit over RNA alone. Config_004 (multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the minimal, direct extension of config_006: it keeps the RNA encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) identical, and only adds an image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) with a standard weighted fusion. This isolates the effect of the image modality. If config_004 substantially outperforms config_006, it confirms image adds signal and justifies further investment in multimodal designs; if it performs similarly or worse, it redirects the search toward RNA-encoder or aggregation improvements. Under a limited budget, resolving this foundational question before exploring encoder variants, fusion strategies, or profile settings is the highest-information next step."
}

